0..67 Comment "// A value beside its code, read at each arm of a case on the code."
68..70 Comment "//"
71..149 Comment "// A two-code universe decodes each code to a type. A case on a code reads the"
150..228 Comment "// goal at each arm\'s code. It also reads each later binder whose type decodes"
229..305 Comment "// the code, so a value typed at the code\'s decode stands at the arm\'s type."
306..308 Comment "//"
309..386 Comment "// The case generalises its motive over the value. The kernel checks the case"
387..447 Comment "// at that motive, and the machine runs the case as written."
448..450 Comment "//"
451..521 Comment "// - see: McBride, _Elimination with a Motive_, TYPES 2000, LNCS 2277,"
522..602 Comment "//   doi:10.1007/3-540-45842-5_13 — a motive generalised over the binders that"
603..631 Comment "//   depend on the scrutinee"
632..706 Comment "// - see: #3483 — refinement by solution, which reads a binder after the"
707..733 Comment "//   scrutinee at each arm"
